A||N||6||Seanh||Can't get valves off heads!||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||11-12-2001||06:31 PM||||I'm trying to take the valves out of a set of heads I have and I can't get them out. I have the spring compressor on there, but it just pushes the valve out the bottem and lets it spin, I can't figure out how to get the retainers out? How's it done?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly - 86 GT<BR>Back to my 3.1L...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||11-12-2001||06:56 PM||||Spray keepers with Liquid Wrench (don't know if it helps, but I use Liquid Wrench on everything - well, except on salads   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).  Put an organic punch (a piece of wood) on the valve head and tap it with a hammer, until the keepers appear (on the other end of the valve, of course).  If the keepers don't fall off by themselves, separate them with a little bitty screwdriver and snag them with a magnet.<P>Hey, your '86 looks just like my 1987 GT.  Except yours is actually clean  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 11-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||11-12-2001||07:00 PM||||Alright, I'll  try that right now...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mark||11-12-2001||07:36 PM||||Are the heads off the engine?  If so, there is nothing to "hold the valves up".  Removing the valves on a naked head is usually done with a spring compressor that counter holds the face of the valve.  You can however use a lever (or puller) type of spring compressor by laying the head down on a block of wood so that the wood holds the valve you intend to remove seated.  <P>Also, you might have to lightly tap on the upper retainer with a small hammer (or wooden dowel, etc) to "unstick" the keepers from the upper retainer and valve stem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||11-12-2001||07:38 PM||||yes, they are off the engine. I haven't gotten off the computer to try messing with them yet, but i will get to them later tonight||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||11-12-2001||09:37 PM||||An old timey method of removing the keepers was to put a socket over the stem ( bigger than the keepers but smaller that the retainers  and give the top of the socket a smack with a hammer. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||11-12-2001||11:46 PM||||Alrighty, that worked perfectly. I got one back off tonight and as soon as I can get the exhaust off I'll do the other side. Thanks||||reg||1
